Z||000003||daved||01-15-2000||07:10 PM||||Dan, Thats a 25 Amp fuse!..if your audio equipment is blowing that...whats it doing to your ears?  Seriously, run for a while without any of your stereo gear connected, and I think you will find the problem gone.  If you reconnect, check for a wire getting warm.  At that current, normal gauge wiring will feel warm to the touch. That might lead you to the culprit. Of course, some of the modern amplifiers, say in the 100Watt range will take 12 to 15 amps on their own. ||||reg||1
